te of East Punjab.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Secretariat Building, Chandigarh","unesco":true,"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/Secretariat_Chandigarh.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/Secretariat_Chandigarh.jpg","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"Sanyam Bahga","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Secretariat_Chandigarh.jpg"}},{"id":"chandigarh_japanese_garden_chandigarh","areaId":"chandigarh","name":"Japanese Garden, Chandigarh","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":30.70453,"lng":76.78206},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"chandigarh_japanese_garden_chandigarh","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":3,"commonsNearby":6,"wikiPageviews":277,"wikidataSitelinks":4,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["japanesegardenchandigarh","chandigarh"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"The Japanese Garden is a park located in Sector 31 in the Union Territory of Chandigarh. Built in 2014 on 13 acres of land by the Indian Government, it was inaugurated by Shivraj Patil on 7 November 2014. It consists of water bodies, pagoda towers, waterfalls, a meditation centre, a Buddha idol, and golden bamboos.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Japanese Garden, Chandigarh","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/The_Japanese_Garden_Chandigarh_scenery.jpg/1280px-The_Japanese_Garden_Chandigarh_scenery.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/The_Japanese_Garden_Chandigarh_scenery.jpg/500px-The_Japanese_Garden_Chandigarh_scenery.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Pankajkukreti03","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Japanese_Garden_Chandigarh_scenery.jpg"}},{"id":"chandigarh_the_legislative_assembly","areaId":"chandi